Ahh, forget Rogue. I'm back to ranger, and I'm loving the sling.
Although I obviously am not perfect at being a Ranger yet... far
from it, considering this especially beginner mistake.

My strategy so far in the early game (i haven't cleared the mines
or Sokoban yet, so early game is all I got :) ), is to find a sling and
a pickaxe in the gnomish mines, run up and chop all the boulders
down to stones and have loads of free amunition in stacks littered
around.

I guess I got screwed by the RNG on this one. 2nd level of Gnomish
mines I find myself surrounded. Fortunatly, I found a /oFire (which
I will now forever call, /oBurning Elbereth). I burned Elbereth on my
square
and launched 60+ stones (I was burdened). After that, a massive group
of
ants spawned while I was still on that 2nd level, so naturally I walked
back
to the Elbereth burned square which was also the staircase.

I walk up the stairs, get another batch of 50+ stones, found an arrow
trap with
50+ arrows in it, killed some gnomes and had ~15 daggers as a result.

Came back down, burdened on the Elbereth square and start sniping the
ants.

Then, an orc shaman spawned with a /oCreate Monster.

No worries I thought. The wand gotta stop eventually... right?

He gets off 1 zap (ants blocking his way and couldn't block), and now
I am surrounded by orcs, more shamans, Ravens, insects, and so forth...
Must have been a cursed wand or something, I was totally surrounded
with
a single zap.

I thought I was invinsible, and thanked the gods for my good luck so
far.
Surrounded by enemies on an Elbereth square, what could go wrong?

Well, the shaman ran away because of Elbereth, and then I heard zaps
~4 or maybe 5 times in the distance. So many enemies the following
happens.

First, I run out of stones (and I destroyed all boulders/statues in
above
levels. No more easy stones till I clear this level)
Then my arrows from that trap.
Then my +0 starting inventory elvish arrows.
Then all my daggers.
Then the other spawned Shamans zapped me with /oStriking to 2 hp.

I retreated to above level, hung around till I got ~15 HP (yeah, I was
an idiot)

Walked back down... expecting the shaman to run away because
I was on Elbereth Square.

He didn't. And a single zap of /oStriking was all it took. DYWYPI?

Oh well, so burned Elbereth =/= invinsible :-(

But I love this sling. Stones are so easy to get, and it is trivial to
get 100+ ammo for the sling when you got a pickaxe. Which is
why I'm sticking to my Ranger till ascension :)

